From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 08:18:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02306/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE D
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment; NEW
 mechanism = a LEARNED FRAME ENCODER) -- does a LEARNED frame encoder (vs the
 GENERIC grid features that nulled in exp4318) carry a game-invariant progress
 signal that transfers cross-game? .399 (exp4318) PROVED generic grid features
 (nonzero/colors/objects/spread/dominant) do NOT transfer cross-game
 (reduction ~1.0, positive control passed) and LOGGED a 'game-invariant ARC
 value representation' gap. research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning
 experiment/milestone; re-measuring generic-feature transfer is churn. The NEW
 mechanism (the gap's candidate fix): train a small LEARNED frame ENCODER (a
 tiny CNN / learned feature map over raw frames, CPU) on the now-11
 reproducibly-solved games' traces, producing a learned embedding the
 value-head consumes; re-test LEAVE-ONE-GAME-OUT cross-game search-efficiency
 transfer (does the learned-encoder value-head reduce OfflineSolver search
 states on a held-out game vs an untrained/uniform heuristic?). POSITIVE
 CONTROL: confirm the baseline solver solves the held-out level
 (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK guard). Report cross_game_state_reduction (held-out
 states_uniform / states_transferred) + per-held-out-game reads + a bootstrap
 CI95. Emit learned_encoder_transfer_helps BARE bool := (reduction > 1.0 AND
 CI95 lower bound > 1.0). verifier_is_oracle=false. A learned-encoder transfer
 where generic features failed CLOSES the gap (a richer game-invariant
 representation); a powered null SHARPENS the gap (the representation is still
 insufficient -> more solved games or a different encoder) and is
 decision-grade. NO TRM training; NO LLM weight mutation (the encoder +
 value-head are a tiny CPU heuristic over solver state).

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
